course: dictionary
lesson: 13578
title: Words for how often
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Some words tell you how often something happens. Incidence is one of them. The incidence of something is how often it happens. «The incidence of flu is high in winter.» This means many people catch flu in winter. The sentence is about how often flu happens.
explain: Look for clue words around incidence. «A high incidence of colds» means colds happen a lot. «A low incidence of colds» means they happen rarely. High and low are the clues, because they tell you the amount. Ask yourself: is the number big or small?
explain: Incidence also has a science meaning. In light and mirrors, the angle of incidence is the angle at which a ray of light hits a surface. The clue is the word angle, and the word ray. Same word, different job: the subject of the lesson tells you which meaning you need.
explain: Try the swap check. Put «how often it happens» in place of incidence. «The how often it happens of flu is high» sounds clumsy, but the meaning still fits. If your swap makes sense, you have the right meaning.
fact: Incidence is a noun: an incidence, incidences (rare).
fact: «Incidence» means how often something happens, such as an illness or a crime.
fact: In science, the angle of incidence is measured from the normal line, an imaginary line at right angles to the surface.
fact: In a mirror, the angle of incidence equals the angle of reflection.
fact: Phrases to know: «a high incidence of», «a low incidence of», «the incidence of disease».
exercise: «The incidence of flu is high in winter.» What does incidence mean here? | *How often flu happens | A place where flu lives | The time of day flu starts | A type of medicine
exercise: «The angle of incidence and the angle of reflection are equal in a mirror.» Which angle is the angle of incidence? | The angle at which light bounces off the mirror | The angle of the mirror on the wall | The angle of the floor under the mirror | *The angle at which light hits the mirror
exercise: In «a high incidence of colds», which word tells you colds happen a lot? | *high | colds | incidence | of
test: «There was a low incidence of accidents on the road this year.» What does incidence mean? | The road itself | *How often accidents happen | The number of cars on the road | A type of accident
test: Ruby says «incidence» is just another word for «incident». What is the best answer? | No, an incidence is a type of car | Yes, an incident is how often something happens | *Not quite: incidence means how often something happens; an incident is one thing that happens | Yes, they mean exactly the same
exam: In science, what is the angle of incidence measured from? | *The normal line, an imaginary line at right angles to the surface | The floor under the mirror | The ray of light after it bounces | The surface of the mirror
